# Three files were committed with CRLF endings while the other 156 use LF. That is a
# historical accident, but rewriting them would bury a real change under a whole-file diff,
# so the endings are declared instead of normalised.
#
# The reason this file exists at all is that `post_tool_review.py` runs `git diff --check`
# after every edit, and git counts the CR in a CRLF line as trailing whitespace. Any edit to
# one of these files therefore failed the post-edit validator and blocked the session --
# including the README update Issue #92 requires. `whitespace=cr-at-eol` tells git the CR is
# intentional here, which is exactly what it means.
#
# New files should use LF. Do not add entries here to make a new CRLF file acceptable;
# normalise the file instead.
README.md whitespace=cr-at-eol
workflow/render_claude_review.py whitespace=cr-at-eol
tests/test_claude_review_render.py whitespace=cr-at-eol
